auxv: answer /proc/self/auxv with a copy that does not name the loader

The kernel records the loader's temp file as AT_EXECFN, which
prctl(PR_GET_AUXV) already answers with the program's own name instead.
Kernels older than 6.4 have no such prctl and are read through
/proc/self/auxv, where the tracee still sees the loader: patching the
result of the read that carries it only works when that read is the next
syscall PRoot happens to stop on, which fopen/fread is not.

Hand out a copy of the vector as a file of its own, so any way of reading
it -- read, pread, a buffered stream -- gets the same answer, and let the
descriptor tracking go.

Offered upstream; drop this file once it lands.
